column7:
Nice device. Been using this for a couple of days and found these observations:

  Battery lasts well over 2 days. Unplugged at 7 AM on Monday and had 35% on Tuesday night. Wifi all thru the day, dozen or so calls, office mails, personal mails, whatsapp, web browsing, music.. this was the general usage. Dont keep the 3G as Wifi was sufficient.

  Wont go into the specs as that is well covered in all other reviews so will point out a few observations. I have purchased this with the optional cover from Lenovo.

  Overall, the software is nothing compared to the simplified Android experience on a Nexus or a Moto handset. Installed Google Now launcher and work pretty well. Heard that with Google UI style from dev options does not allow OTA updates.

  Speaker is good enough but not stereophonic. Should be on the upgrade list for the next version by Lenovo - place 2 speakers on the front!!

  The cover works like a smart cover and beats tapping the power button to switch on or off... but, the phone's ergonomics are such that the power button is not easy to press while with the cover.

  The cover does have soft areas to take care of the volume rocker on the opposite side but the little plastic screen is a finger print magnet on both sides.

  The cover is fold-able and allows the phone to be kept in landscape without slipping.

  The bundled headphones are adequate and the mic picks voice pretty well. It is a flat cable and does not tangle easy. More OEMs should go with the this type of cable as really can get frustrating to untangle every time.

  I've not tried any otg memory devices yet and the onboard 32GB has been sufficient. Oh.. the reports of heating on other forums and review, I've not experienced any of that. Yes, it will get warm but not HOT as has been panned earlier.


  What would make this better device would be to do away with Vibe UI and like Moto, go with stock Android;

  Expandable memory - seems most new Google devices are starting to move away from expandable memory for whatever reasons;

  Better headphones - this has the same quality as those on an older P780. Not bad but definitely old;

  Give a clear road-map for updates. Forget Lollipop, let your customers know how long you will support updates, similar to HTC Advantage program;

  Reduce the bloatware - no one will loose sleep if the device does not come with Lenovo Security and unnecessary games. We can all install them if we want to;

  Allow people to remove apps if we want to and install from the Play Store later if required - no brainer;

  SyncIT is a good package but needs to be updated to transfer applications and the application data as well - WhatsApp in particular. Right now only has option of contacts, sms and call logs;

  Is there a setting hidden away to change the mini display while using the flipcover? Have not seen that. would be nice to have that feature.



